# Anything executed inside the Linux image must keep LF endings regardless of the
# platform it was checked out on. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) both
# `git archive` and a plain `docker build` off the working tree otherwise ship
# `#!/bin/sh\r`, and the container dies on start with the singularly unhelpful
#
#     exec ./docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# -- the file is right there; it is the \r on the shebang that cannot be resolved.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
